--- (3) THE STEP TEST ---
  PRIMARY step: rise side (R < 6.1, mean beta +0.159 +- 0.068)
    vs fall side (6.74-8.78, mean beta -0.062 +- 0.023)
    -> STEP = +0.221 beta units, formal sigma 3.07
  2-pair scan: max step +0.158 at cut in [5.98, 6.48] kpc (mid 6.22), formal sigma 1.40
  beta sign flip (rise -> fall) in ONE bin gap at r = 6.22 kpc
    |d beta| = 0.095 beta units  formal sigma 0.63
    empirical z vs well-measured adjacent-jump scatter elsewhere (R in 5.3-18.2, n = 22) = -0.1  (MAD-z -0.2; median elsewhere 0.117, std 0.320)
  the curve's PEAK (parabola, bins 5.27-7.22): r_peak = 6.33 kpc, 68% CI 6.15-6.56
    bootstrap P(peak in [6.1, 6.74]) = 80.2%  (n = 4000)

