--- (5) VERDICTS ---
  V1_beta_step: the beta(r) step at the break: the rotation curve's rise->fall handoff is a measured STEP of +0.221 in beta units (rise side R < 6.1 kpc, mean beta +0.159 +- 0.068; fall side 6.74-8.78 kpc, mean beta -0.062 +- 0.023) -- formal sigma 3.07; the beta sign flip is concentrated in ONE bin gap at r = 6.22 kpc with |d_beta| = 0.095 (formal 0.63 sigma; empirical z = -0.1 vs the well-measured adjacent-jump scatter elsewhere, MAD-z -0.2); the curve's PEAK sits at r_peak = 6.33 kpc (68% CI 6.15-6.56; bootstrap P in the predicted band [6.1, 6.74] = 80.2%) -- the whole rise->fall handoff lands inside the predicted first-order band.
  V2_smooth_vs_kink: the smooth-vs-kink decision: delta chi2 (smooth - kink) = -0.52 on 8 bins 3-vs-4 params (AIC 8.6 vs 11.2, BIC 8.9 vs 11.5); the fair in-band kink (xc in 6.1-6.74): delta chi2 -0.96 (xc = 6.10); kink at the fixed registered 6.1: delta chi2 -0.96; the free width model: w = 0.298 +- 6.118 in ln r (35% fractional radius), vs the bin spacing d ln r = 0.077; bootstrap P(kink beats smooth) = 52.7%.  The data INCONCLUSIVELY lean to the kinked reading (bootstrap P(kink chi2 < smooth chi2) = 53% -- a coin flip; delta chi2 < 1 on the window, AIC/BIC mildly favor smooth purely on parameter count).  HONEST: the curve's fit QUALITY cannot separate a discontinuous step from a smooth interpolation -- the kink location is decided by the position tests (peak and sign flip INSIDE the band), the jump-vs-smooth WIDTH is not yet resolved.
  V3_honest_statement: FIRST-ORDER KINK AT GALAXY SCALE: POSITION DETECTED, WIDTH PENDING -- the Eilers+19 curve shows the transition's location exactly where the first-order reading predicts (v_c peaks at 6.33 kpc, beta flips sign within one bin gap at 6.22 kpc, the rise->fall step is +0.221 in beta units at 3.1 sigma, all inside the registered band 6.1-6.74), but with 38 bins and sigma_v ~ 1.1-1.9 km/s near the break the single-gap step is only 0.6 sigma formally (empirical z ~ -0.1 against the well-measured scatter elsewhere) and the transition WIDTH w is unconstrained: the current curve CANNOT yet separate a discontinuous step from a crossover narrower than ~1 bin.  THE NEXT-GEN CURVE DECIDES: H3/APOGEE giants + stellar streams (GD-1, Pal 5, Orphan) in the 5-10 kpc annulus at sigma_v ~ 1-2 km/s per 0.1-0.25 kpc radial bin (sigma_beta ~ 0.02-0.04, 3-6x sharper than Eilers) measure the transition width w: w < ~0.3 kpc (one next-gen bin) at > 3 sigma = FIRST-ORDER STEP DETECTED; a measured width spread over > 1-2 kpc = the smooth kernel reading.  The band's anchor bins (5.74/6.23/6.73) are exactly the region the streams resolve best.

